       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. The usual maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use.\n- **Single dose:** 1,600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Risks:** A dose this high raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCommon regimens are:\n- 400\u2013800 mg PO three or four times daily, with a maximum of 3,200 mg/day.\n- 1,600 mg total per day, for example 400 mg four times daily. This may be what was meant.\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,600 mg four times daily, please confirm that it's intended and give the clinical rationale. I would still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
